"],["_keyring_username","m2c/src/m2c/auth/credentials.py::_keyring_username"],["log_event","m2c/src/m2c/logging_setup.py::log_event"],["CredentialStoreError","m2c/src/m2c/auth/credentials.py::CredentialStoreError"]],"cc":8,"cc_deep":8,"code":27,"decorators":[],"doc":true,"doc1":"Remove the stored credential from both places.","end":561,"hash":"45a58bf8d6","kind":"function","loc":35,"name":"delete_credential","params":[{"annotation":"Mapping[str, str] | None","default":"None","name":"environ"}],"qual":"delete_credential","raises":["CredentialStoreError"],"returns":"bool","start":527,"test":false,"visibility":"public"}],"git":{"added":561,"commits":1,"dates":["2026-10-25"],"deleted":0,"first":"2026-10-25","last":"2026-10-25"},"lang":"python","lines":561,"module_doc":"m2c/src/m2c/auth/credentials.py -- Patch C03: the device credential, where it\nis kept on this machine, and the error types of the whole ``auth`` package.\n\nWHAT A DEVICE CREDENTIAL IS\n---------------------------\n``m2c login`` (login.py) ends with the server handing this device one long\nrandom string, exactly once (S03, backend/eo/devices.py: 256 random bits, only\nits SHA-256 is stored server side).  That string is the thing that\nauthenticates the device from then on:\n\n* ``get_access_token()`` (login.py) exchanges it for a ~15 minute JWT for\n  plain HTTP calls;\n* C04's device link sends it in the socket's ``hello`` message\n  (protocol/v1/hello.json ``device_credential``), because P00 authenticates\n  the socket with the credential itself and there is no JWT on it.  C04 reads\n  it with ``load_credential()`` below.\n\nBesides the secret, the record carries the ``device_id`` the server assigned\nand the ``server_url`` that issued it.  The URL matters: a credential must only\never be sent to the server that issued it (see ``ServerMismatchError`` in\nlogin.py), so it is stored with the credential rather than trusted from the\nenvironment at the moment of use.\n\nWHERE IT IS KEPT\n----------------\n1. The OS keyring, when the optional ``keyring`` package is installed\n   (``pip install 'm2c[keyring]'``) AND it has a usable backend.  The module is\n   imported lazily and is never required; keyring's own \"fail\" backend, which\n   is what a stock WSL2 install ends up with (build plan §11.1: Secret Se","path":"m2c/src/m2c/auth/credentials.py","size":23607,"test":false},{"binary":false,"blank":116,"classes":[{"bases":["urllib.request.HTTPRedirectHandler"],"decorators":[],"doc":true,"doc1":"Never follow a redirect: it could move the pairing to another host or downgrade it.","end":216,"hash":"79696e2e64","loc":6,"method_names":["redirect_request"],"methods":1,"name":"_NoRedirect","qual":"_NoRedirect","start":211},{"bases":[],"decorators":["dataclass"],"doc":true,"doc1":"What one POST amounted to.","end":231,"fields":[{"name":"kind","type":"str"},{"name":"status","type":"int"},{"name":"body","type":"Secret | None"},{"name":"retry_after","type":"int | None"}],"hash":"256b968f56","loc":9,"method_names":[],"methods":0,"name":"_Outcome","qual":"_Outcome","start":223},{"bases":[],"decorators":["dataclass(frozen=True)"],"doc":false,"end":333,"fields":[{"name":"device_code","type":"Secret"},{"name":"user_code","type":"str"},{"name":"verification_url","type":"str"},{"name":"interval","type":"int"},{"name":"lifetime","type":"int"}],"hash":"520b7721a7","loc":6,"method_names":[],"methods":0,"name":"_StartReply","qual":"_StartReply","start":328},{"bases":[],"decorators":["dataclass"],"doc":false,"end":453,"fields":[{"name":"device_id","type":"str"},{"name":"device_name","type":"str"},{"name":"storage","type":"str"}],"hash":"4f03d4a2f0","loc":4,"method_names":[],"methods":0,"name":"LoginResult","qual":"LoginResult","start":450},{"bases":[],"decorators":["dataclass(frozen=True)"],"doc":false,"end":684,"fields":[{"name":"key","type":"str"},{"name":"token","type":"Secret"},{"name":"refresh_at","type":"float"}],"hash":"2251f4bb7d","loc":4,"method_names":[],"methods":0,"name":"_Cache